I\'92m very interested in attending AAPOR next year. It\'92s been an important part of my professional community and a great opportunity to network with other researchers, stay connected with the field, and learn about new methodological developments. I\'92m especially looking forward to next year\'92s theme and the roundtable discussions. I always learn something from these, and they\'92re a great way to broaden my thinking and bring ideas back to our work at Pew.\
\
Beyond my routine ATP production work, I\'92ve started thinking about a couple of methodological areas, including appending voter files to survey data and modeling survey completion propensities using data from past waves to improve completion projections. Since I just started, I likely won\'92t have a fully developed abstract ready by the submission deadline. I\'92d like to explore these ideas further, though, and would also be happy to contribute to a collaborative project if anyone on the Domestic Methods team is planning to submit.\
\
